  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 127 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nWednesday through Friday, the aforementioned upper level ridge will \nbegin to shift west, closer to Texas. Although the ridge is forecast \nto get closer to the forecast area during this time frame it is also \nforecast to weaken. This will result in a continuation of above \nnormal temperatures, but temperatures should be slightly less hot \nthan what is forecast at the beginning of the week. Expect highs in \nthe mid 90s to near 100, with highs trending down by about a degree \nor two every day. \n\nA pattern change is forecast to take shape as we head into the \nweekend. An upper level trough is forecast to strengthen across the \nwestern CONUS, helping to break down the upper level ridge that has \nbeen dominating our weather. This will result in cooler temperatures \nand an increase in rain chances. Highs on Saturday will still be in \nthe mid 90s, with highs Sunday down into the low to mid 90s. There \ncontinues to be uncertainty on the eventual position and strength of \nthe trough to our west this weekend (into early next week), so for \nnow low to medium (20-50%) rain chances were kept in the forecast.",
